Turn the "git" flavor into the shell package nexora patches.

Unmodified, `assembleGitContinuous` builds the client, the menu and the server
through the externalNativeBuild block and packages all of them into the APK:
38 MB, of which libclient is 6.5 MB and libmenu 6.3 MB per ABI. Nexora injects
its own build of both into this package after download (the patch log shows
"+ libclient_android_arm64.so"), so neither copy is ever loaded.

The engine looks for the menu as cl_dlls/libmenu_android_<arch>.so, then
<gamelibdir>/libmenu_android_<arch>.so, then libmenu.so from its own package -
never a copy inside the client APK - and the client dll is dlopen'ed out of the
injected set. The APK only has to be a launchable shell.

The server side goes for the same reason: yapb and ReGameDLL_CS get pulled
into the Android build graph but land in neither the APK nor nexora's Android
bundle, so they were minutes of compiling for nothing.

minSdk moves 21 -> 24 because the libraries nexora injects are cross-compiled
against API 24; an APK claiming 21 would install on a device that cannot load
what gets injected into it.

The game content (~26 MB) is deliberately not added: nexora installs it into
the game directory from its own bundle, so a second copy is pure download
weight. android/ci/build-amxx.sh builds the real libclient/libmenu for the
bundles, from this same pinned tree.

Applied by the "Build the client APK" step, so it is tied to the commit in
cs16-client.pin rather than to a fork of it.

diff --git a/android/app/build.gradle b/android/app/build.gradle
index 016139f..0f4b6d5 100644
--- a/android/app/build.gradle
+++ b/android/app/build.gradle
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ android {
 		applicationId = "su.xash.cs16client"
 		versionName = "1.35-" + getGitHash()
 		versionCode = getBuildNum()
-		minSdk = 21
+		minSdk = 24
 		targetSdk = 36
 
 		ndk {
@@ -97,6 +97,31 @@ android {
 		create("git") {
 			dimension = "version"
 			buildConfigField("Boolean", "IS_GOOGLE_PLAY_BUILD", "false")
+
+			// Without an abiFilters block AGP builds every ABI the NDK
+			// supports, so the APK carried lib/x86 and lib/x86_64 copies of
+			// the client that nothing can load. Nexora only ever produced
+			// the arm64-v8a and armeabi-v7a bundles, so an x86 install
+			// never got a cl_dll from anywhere.
+			ndk {
+				abiFilters "arm64-v8a", "armeabi-v7a"
+			}
+
+			packaging {
+				jniLibs {
+					// useLegacyPackaging stores .so uncompressed, which is
+					// what the engine needs for the libraries nexora injects
+					// into this package: they are dlopen'ed straight out of
+					// the APK, so extractNativeLibs=false has to stay.
+					useLegacyPackaging = true
+				}
+			}
+
+			externalNativeBuild {
+				cmake {
+					arguments "-DBUILD_CLIENT=OFF", "-DBUILD_SERVER=OFF", "-DBUILD_MAINUI=OFF"
+				}
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
